# Placeholders for the new maps (new maps, 2026-11-10): one quiet card for each new place, so a visit always shows
# something until the place's own cards are written (docs/maps-plan.md). Low weight, so real cards win; tagged
# `placeholder`, so lint lists them instead of judging them. Each is retired (`when: false`) once its place has cards.

@pool maps_placeholder
class: routine
tone: warm
repeat: 1
weight: 2
tags: placeholder

@event capital_library_quiet_hour
title: The Reading Room
pool: maps_placeholder
place: royal_library_archives
art: book
scene: A vast reading room under a glass dome, green lamps on long tables, a few readers bent over their books in the hush.
text: Upstairs from the archives, the Royal Library keeps a reading room for anyone who can whisper. The lamps are green, the chairs are hard and a librarian watches the door like a cat at a mousehole.
> left: Read a while
  lore +tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: {~An hour with a book you couldn't get at Lumenhold, and then the closing bell, three chapters from the end. You'll never know how it ends.|You read until the librarian's look becomes a cough, and the cough becomes your name, said aloud to the whole silent room. It was nearly worth it.}
> right: Just look at the dome
  mood +tiny
  say: {~You stand under the dome until your neck aches, then go out into the noise again.|Light falls through the glass in long dusty bars. You leave without reading a word.}

@event capital_townhouse_quiet_hour
title: The Front Steps
pool: maps_placeholder
place: capital_townhouse
art: house
scene: Polished front steps of a tall uptown townhouse, a brass knocker shaped like a crest, the street busy with carriages below.
text: The townhouse is quiet: the family is out, the cook has gone to her sister's and the steps have just been scrubbed. You could sit on them, if anyone sat on steps uptown.
> left: Sit on the steps anyway
  mood +tiny
  renown -tiny
  say: {~You sit. Two carriages slow down to look. You wave. They don't.|The step is still warm from the day. A neighbour's footman pretends not to see you, very loudly.}
> right: Go in and rest
  health +tiny
  say: {~Your old room, a cool sheet, the clock in the hall. You sleep an hour you didn't plan.|The house is so quiet you can hear the clock two floors down. You rest, and nobody asks you anything.}

# Retired (C2): the place has its own cards (maps/capital_society.grim).
@event capital_club_quiet_hour
title: The Porter's Look
when: false
pool: maps_placeholder
place: capital_club
art: cup
scene: A dim club entrance of dark wood and brass, a porter in a waistcoat at a high desk looking a student up and down.
text: The members' club has a porter whose whole job is to decide who you are. He looks at your boots, then at your face, then at your boots again. "Members only, unless you're expected."
> left: Say you're expected
  renown +tiny
  alignment -tiny
  say: {~"By whom?" You name a patron off a portrait in the hall. He lets you as far as the cloakroom, which is more than most get.|He doesn't believe you, but he admires the attempt. You get a glass of water and a better story than you came in with.}
> right: Thank him and go
  mood -tiny
  say: {~"Another time," he says, which means never, said kindly.|You leave. Through the window, someone laughs in a chair that costs more than your year.}

# Retired (S1): the bazaar and the arcade have their own cards (maps/capital_markets.grim).
@event capital_bazaar_quiet_hour
title: A Hundred Stalls
when: false
pool: maps_placeholder
place: capital_bazaar
art: coin
scene: A vast covered market, light falling through high windows onto stalls of spices, maps, brass and coloured glass, crowds moving between them.
text: The Grand Bazaar is one long noise under a glass roof: spice-sellers, map-dealers, a woman selling birds that sing in other languages. You could lose an afternoon here. You could lose a purse.
> left: Wander and look
  mood +tiny
  gold -tiny
  say: {~You come out with a paper of sugared almonds and no idea where the afternoon went.|A map-seller lets you hold a chart of a coast nobody has sailed. You buy a pastry to recover.}
> right: Keep your hand on your purse
  say: {~You walk the length of it with a hand on your purse and see almost nothing. Your purse thanks you.|You watch a pickpocket work a whole aisle. Educational.}

# Retired (S1): the bazaar and the arcade have their own cards (maps/capital_markets.grim).
@event capital_arcade_quiet_hour
title: Brass Plates
when: false
pool: maps_placeholder
place: capital_arcade
art: scroll
scene: A long stone colonnade of open doors and polished brass nameplates, a bathhouse's steam drifting out of one archway.
text: The arcade sells everything that isn't a thing: a physician, a tutor, a scribe, a bathhouse, a portraitist and a fortune-teller who is, her plate says, "by appointment, mostly". Today you only read the plates.
> left: Steam at the bathhouse
  gold -tiny
  health +tiny
  say: {~The bathhouse is hot, tiled and full of retired admirals. You come out new.|Steam, cold plunge, steam again. Your shoulders forget the term.}
> right: Read the plates and walk on
  mood +tiny
  say: {~"Teeth drawn, letters written, futures read." You admire the ambition and walk on.|You read every plate twice. One just says "No."}

# Retired (C2): the place has its own cards (maps/capital_society.grim).
@event capital_theatre_quiet_hour
title: Gilt and Draughts
when: false
pool: maps_placeholder
place: capital_theatre
art: mask
scene: The foyer of a grand gilded theatre, chandeliers half-lit, a playbill being pasted on a pillar by a stagehand on a ladder.
text: The theatre is between shows: chandeliers half-lit, the foyer smelling of dust and oranges. A stagehand on a ladder is pasting up a new playbill and getting most of the paste on himself.
> left: Hold his ladder
  mood +tiny
  say: {~He gives you a ticket for the gods in thanks. The gods are very high and very cheap and you love them.|You hold the ladder; he tells you which actress hates which. It's better than the play.}
> right: Read the playbill
  charm +tiny
  say: {~You learn the names off by heart, in case anyone asks. Nobody does, but you're ready.|A tragedy, a farce and a farce pretending to be a tragedy. You'd see all three.}

@event capital_guild_quiet_hour
title: The Hiring Hall
pool: maps_placeholder
place: alchemists_works
art: cauldron
scene: A bare hiring hall at the gate of a great riverside works, a chalkboard of jobs, chimneys smoking beyond the window.
text: The Guild works' hiring hall is a bench, a chalkboard and a foreman who looks at hands, not faces. Today the board says "NOTHING" in large letters, and under it, in smaller ones, "try tomorrow".
> left: Wait in case
  mood -tiny
  alchemy +tiny
  say: {~Nothing comes up, but the old hands on the bench argue about distillation for an hour and you listen to every word.|You wait. You learn three words for a burst vat, none polite.}
> right: Come back another day
  say: {~"Tomorrow," the foreman says, which is what he says.|You leave the bench to the regulars.}

# Retired (C3): the place has its own cards (maps/capital_port.grim).
@event capital_docks_quiet_hour
title: Gulls and Cranes
when: false
pool: maps_placeholder
place: capital_docks
art: wave
scene: Busy harbour wharves at the river's mouth, cranes swinging crates off a tall ship, gulls wheeling over stacked barrels.
text: Port Calder's docks never stop: cranes, barrels, a ship from somewhere hot unloading something that smells of oranges. A boy offers to mind your bag for a penny, which is how bags go missing.
> left: Pay the boy
  gold -tiny
  mood +tiny
  say: {~He minds it beautifully and tells you which ships are smuggling. All of them, apparently.|Your bag comes back with everything in it and one extra orange. Business is business.}
> right: Keep your bag
  guile +tiny
  say: {~You keep your bag and watch the boy offer the same deal to a sailor, who laughs and pays. You learn something.|"Suit yourself." He's gone before you see him go.}

@event capital_counting_house_quiet_hour
title: The Tide Under the Floor
pool: maps_placeholder
time: evening night
when: slot == "evening" or slot == "night"
place: capital_counting_house
art: coin
scene: A counting house on a wharf after hours, the high desks empty, an old night porter lighting a lantern by the door, water glinting through gaps in the floorboards.
text: After hours the counting house is yours again: empty desks, the smell of ink, and at high water the tide coming right in under the floor, slapping the piles. The night porter is lighting his lantern for his round of the moorings. He's been doing it since you were small enough to carry it.
> left: Walk the moorings with him
  mood +small
  health -tiny
  say: {~You carry the lantern again, as if you were eight. He tells you which ropes are new and which ships are late. The wind off the water gets into your bones.|The round of the moorings, rope by rope. The porter's knees are worse; your lantern is steadier. The cold walks home with you.}
> right: Go up and rest
  health +tiny
  say: {~Your old room still smells of ink. You sleep to the sound of the tide under the floor.|Upstairs, the noise of the wharf is a lullaby you'd forgotten.}

@event capital_crew_loft_quiet_hour
title: The Chandler's Downstairs
pool: maps_placeholder
place: capital_crew_loft
art: house
scene: A chandler's shop under a loft, coils of rope and barrels of tar, an old chandler at his counter pointedly not looking up at the ceiling, which creaks.
text: Under the loft is the chandler's: rope, tar, lamp-oil and an old man who has spent thirty years not knowing what goes on over his ceiling. He nods to you as if you'd been out for bread. "They're up there," he says. "I don't know anything about it."
> left: Mind his counter an hour
  gold +tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: {~You sell a coil of rope, two lamps and a tin of tar to a captain who calls you "boy" and "miss" in the same sentence. The chandler gives you a coin and a look of mild surprise.|An hour behind the counter, measuring rope by the fathom. Your hands smell of tar till morning, and there's a coin in it.}
> right: Sleep in your old hammock
  health +tiny
  say: {~The hammock still knows your shape. You sleep through the stove smoke and an argument about a dog.|You sleep like you used to, with one hand on your boots.}

@event countryside_mill_quiet_hour
title: The Turning Wheel
# Retired (K2): the mill village has cards of its own.
when: false
pool: maps_placeholder
place: countryside_mill
art: wave
scene: A mill on a slow river in a small grey village, its wheel turning, children skipping a rope on the green in front of the chapel.
text: The mill wheel turns slowly, the chapel stands small and grey, and on the green the children skip to a rhyme with a lot of counting in it. They stop when you come near, and smile, and start again when you've passed.
> left: Watch the wheel a while
  mood +tiny
  say: {~The wheel goes round, the water goes over, and the afternoon goes with it.|You watch the wheel until you notice the river is lower than the wheel is fast. Probably nothing.}
> right: Walk on through
  say: {~The village waves you off. All of it.|You walk on. Behind you, the skipping starts again, counting.}

@event countryside_marsh_quiet_hour
title: Lights on the Water
# Retired (K1): the Marsh has cards of its own.
when: false
pool: maps_placeholder
place: countryside_marsh
art: leaf
scene: Reed beds and black water at dusk, small pale lights hanging low over the marsh, a house on stilts at its edge.
text: The Marsh is reeds, black water and a path that's there until it isn't. At dusk, little lights come out and hang over the pools. A house on stilts stands at the edge with a lamp in its window.
> left: Watch the lights from the path
  mood +tiny
  lore +tiny
  say: {~The lights drift together and apart, as if they're talking. You don't follow them, which is the main thing.|One light comes nearer than the others. You keep to the path, and it goes away, disappointed.}
> right: Turn back before dark
  say: {~You turn back while the path is still a path.|You leave the Marsh to its lights.}

@event countryside_moors_quiet_hour
title: The Third Cairn
# Retired (K3): the moor's own cards, and the delve's edge carries the shepherd's warning.
when: false
pool: maps_placeholder
place: countryside_moors
art: paw
scene: Open moorland of heather and grey stone cairns, fog rising in the hollows, a lone sheep watching from a rock.
text: The moors go on longer than they should. A shepherd tells you to stay this side of the third cairn, then walks off before you can ask why. Fog is coming up in the hollows, unhurried.
> left: Walk to the first cairn and back
  health -tiny
  mood +tiny
  say: {~The wind is clean and enormous. You touch the cairn, count to ten, and come back with your cheeks burning.|You reach the first cairn. The second is closer than it looked. You turn back anyway.}
> right: Stay by the road
  say: {~You watch the fog fill the hollows from the road, which is the sensible place to watch it from.|A sheep stares at you until you leave. You leave.}

@event countryside_ridge_quiet_hour
title: The Stones
# Retired (K2): the ridge has cards of its own.
when: false
pool: maps_placeholder
place: countryside_ridge
art: planet
scene: A ring of grey standing stones on a bare ridge under a huge sky, the valley's villages small and far below.
text: The stones on the ridge stand in a ring, leaning a little, as if listening to the valley. From up here you can see both villages, the fen and the moors, and the road joining them like a stitch.
> left: Count the stones
  lore +tiny
  say: {~You count them twice and get two answers. You decide it's the wind.|Nineteen, you think. Or twenty. You stop counting.}
> right: Just take in the view
  mood +tiny
  say: {~The whole valley, small and peaceful, from up here. It looks very well kept.|The wind tugs your coat and the villages smoke quietly below. Nothing up here wants anything from you.}

@event travel_city_morning
title: A Morning in the Capital
pool: maps_placeholder
plan: travel_city
art: coin
scene: Early morning in a capital city, a student at a lodging-house window looking down at barrows, bells and smoke.
text: The capital wakes before you do, and louder: barrows, bells, a man selling hot chestnuts under your window as if his life depends on it, which it may.
> left: Chestnuts for breakfast
  gold -tiny
  mood +tiny
  say: {~They burn your fingers and taste of smoke and autumn. A good start.|You eat them walking, like a native, and get lost like a visitor.}
> right: Plan the day over cheap tea
  lore +tiny
  say: {~You draw a map of the day on the back of a playbill. The capital ignores it completely.|Cheap tea, a borrowed newspaper, a plan. Good enough.}

@event travel_country_morning
title: A Morning in the Countryside
pool: maps_placeholder
plan: travel_country
art: leaf
scene: Early morning in a country village, mist on the fields, a student at a window watching a farmer lead a cart down the lane.
text: The country wakes slowly: a cart in the lane, mist on the fields, a rooster with opinions. Your host has left bread and a jug of milk outside your door, and a sprig of something green tied round the jug.
> left: Breakfast at the window
  mood +tiny
  say: {~The bread is still warm. The mist lifts off the fields like a lid.|You eat slowly, watching the village wake. Everyone waves at your window.}
> right: Walk out early
  health +tiny
  say: {~You walk the lane before anyone is up. The fields are very quiet, and the scarecrows are very well dressed.|An early walk, wet boots, and the whole valley to yourself.}

# ---------------- Round 2 (2026-11-11): the new pins, until their batches land ----------------

@event vaneshade_house_quiet_hour
title: The Black Seal
pool: maps_placeholder
place: vaneshade_house
art: crown
scene: A tall black-stone house on a curving uptown street, a black wax seal carved in stone over its door, a footman on the step.
text: The footman at Vaneshade House looks at your boots, then at your face, then at your boots again. Miss Vaneshade, he says, is at her practice and not receiving.
> left: Leave your name
  charm +tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: {~He takes your name on a silver tray as if it might stain it. Somewhere upstairs, a window opens.|You leave your name. The door shuts with the soft, expensive sound of a door that has shut on better people.}
> right: Walk on along the Crescent
  mood +tiny
  say: {~You walk the curve of the Crescent, all black stone and white steps, and feel underdressed in a pleasant, distant way.|You walk on. Behind you, someone in an upstairs window lets a curtain fall.}

@event oracle_rooms_quiet_hour
title: The Queue on the Stairs
pool: maps_placeholder
place: oracle_rooms
art: eye
scene: A hushed upper staircase lined with anxious, well-dressed petitioners waiting on a bench outside a closed double door.
text: The stairs to the Oracle's Rooms are full of people in good coats pretending not to be nervous. A clerk takes names. Nobody speaks above a whisper, in case the future is listening.
> left: Wait with them a while
  lore +tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: {~You wait an hour. A man comes out white-faced and a woman comes out laughing. Neither will say what they heard.|You wait. The clerk calls a name that isn't yours, and then, oddly, looks straight at you.}
> right: Leave them to it
  mood +tiny
  say: {~You go back down into the street, where the future is somebody else's business.|You leave. On the stairs, a duchess is crying quietly into a very good glove.}

@event hollis_house_quiet_hour
title: The Brass Plate
pool: maps_placeholder
place: hollis_house
art: house
scene: A narrow, immaculate uptown house with a polished brass nameplate on the door and perfectly straight window boxes.
text: Hollis House has the straightest window boxes in the street and a brass plate polished until it squints back at you. {slot == "noon": Someone inside is practising scales on a piano, very correctly.|Behind the curtains, someone is reading aloud, very correctly.}
> left: Knock
  charm +tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: {~A maid answers, says the family is at {slot == "noon": luncheon|{slot == "evening": dinner|tea}}, and shuts the door with great precision.|Nobody answers, but the {slot == "noon": piano|reading} stops, and starts again exactly where it left off.}
> right: Pass by
  mood +tiny
  say: {~You pass by. The {slot == "noon": piano follows you to the corner, exactly in time|reading voice follows you to the corner, not missing a comma}.|You walk on. Even the cobbles outside look as if they've been told to sit up straight.}

# Retired (C2): the place has its own cards (maps/capital_society.grim).
@event capital_gardens_quiet_hour
title: The Promenade
when: false
pool: maps_placeholder
place: capital_gardens
art: flower
scene: A gravel promenade between clipped hedges and a fountain in a city park, fashionable walkers strolling slowly, a hothouse glittering behind.
text: Everyone uptown walks the Royal Gardens at this hour, slowly, in their best, nodding to the people they've decided to nod to. The fountain is the only thing in a hurry.
> left: Promenade with them
  renown +tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: {~You walk the loop twice, nodding at the right moments. A dowager nods back, then asks a companion who you are.|You promenade. Your feet hurt and three people now know your face.}
> right: Sit by the fountain
  mood +small
  say: {~You sit on the fountain's edge and watch the city pretend to relax.|The spray drifts over you. For a moment the capital is quiet.}

# Retired (C3): the place has its own cards (maps/capital_port.grim).
@event capital_cathedral_quiet_hour
title: Under the Lamp
when: false
pool: maps_placeholder
place: capital_cathedral
art: candle
scene: The vast dim nave of a cathedral, a single great lamp burning high above the altar, a few worshippers and visitors in the pews.
text: The cathedral swallows the city's noise at the door. High over the altar the Lamp burns, as it has for four hundred years, and the light it gives is warmer than it has any right to be.
> left: Sit under the Lamp
  mood +small
  health -tiny
  say: {~You sit a long while on a cold pew and think about nothing useful. It's the best hour of the day, stiff back and all.|You sit until the bells ring the hour overhead and the whole building hums with it, and your knees have gone numb.}
> right: Read the old memorials
  lore +tiny
  say: {~Brass plates in the floor, names worn smooth by four centuries of feet. One is a Lumenhold headmaster's.|You read the memorials along the aisle: admirals, bakers, a famous duellist, a dog.}

# Retired (C3): the place has its own cards (maps/capital_port.grim).
@event capital_printing_row_quiet_hour
title: Hot Off the Press
when: false
pool: maps_placeholder
place: capital_printing_row
art: paper
scene: A narrow street of print shops, presses thumping behind open doors, a boy running past with a stack of fresh broadsheets.
text: Printing Row thumps like a heart. Every door has a press behind it and every press is printing something somebody will regret. A boy runs past shouting tomorrow's headline today.
> left: Buy a broadsheet
  gold -tiny
  lore +tiny
  say: {~The ink comes off on your fingers. The news is a scandal you've never heard of, involving a duke and a swan.|You read it on a step. Somebody uptown is suing somebody else for a portrait.}
> right: Watch the presses
  mood +tiny
  say: {~A printer lets you watch from the door. The press bangs, the sheet lifts, and the city's morning is made.|You watch letters set backwards, very fast, by a girl who never looks down.}

# Retired (C2): the place has its own cards (maps/capital_society.grim).
@event capital_bridges_quiet_hour
title: Lamps on the Bridges
when: false
pool: maps_placeholder
place: capital_bridges
art: lantern
scene: An old stone bridge over a river at dusk crowded with buskers and walkers, a lamplighter on a ladder lighting the lamps one by one.
text: At dusk the lamplighters come out along the bridges with their long poles, and the lamps go on one by one above the buskers, the hawkers and the couples who have come to watch them do it.
> left: Drop a coin for a busker
  gold -tiny
  mood +small
  say: {~A fiddler plays you a jig for a penny, and a whole tune for the look on your face.|You toss a coin to a juggler with five burning torches. He catches it with his teeth.}
> right: Watch the lamps come on
  mood +tiny
  say: {~One by one, all the way down the river, until the water is full of lamps too.|You watch the last lamp lit. The lamplighter tips his hat to it, as if it had done him a favour.}

@event ten_clockworks_quiet_hour
title: Forty Clocks
pool: maps_placeholder
place: ten_clockworks
art: gear
scene: A cluttered clockmaker's workshop full of ticking clocks on every wall, a long workbench covered in tiny gears and brass tools.
text: The Ten Clockworks' shop has forty clocks on its walls, and they all strike the hour within a breath of each other, which in this family counts as a disagreement.
> left: Look at the clocks
  arcana +tiny
  say: {~One clock runs backwards. A small card under it says NOT FOR SALE (A HOBBY).|You lean close to the smallest clock. It's built into a thimble, and it's right.}
> right: Step back out
  mood +tiny
  say: {~You leave before the hour strikes. Behind you, forty clocks argue about it.|You go out into the works smoke. The ticking follows you down the street.}

# Retired (C3): the place has its own cards (maps/capital_port.grim).
@event capital_coaching_yard_quiet_hour
title: Coaches In
when: false
pool: maps_placeholder
place: capital_coaching_yard
art: map
scene: A busy cobbled coaching yard, horses steaming, porters hauling trunks off the roof of a mud-spattered coach, travellers milling.
text: A coach from the north rolls in spattered to the windows, and the yard fills with trunks, horses, porters and people trying to remember which of the trunks is theirs.
> left: Lend a porter a hand
  vigor +tiny
  health -tiny
  say: {~You hoist a trunk off the roof. It's full of books, or bricks. The porter shares his tip with you.|You carry a hatbox the size of a small sheep. Its owner tips you a coin and a stern look.}
> right: Watch the travellers
  lore +tiny
  say: {~A man in furs, a girl with a caged owl, a whole family of fiddlers. Everyone arriving looks lost and hopeful.|You watch them come in. Somebody always gets off looking for someone who isn't there.}

# Retired (C3): the place has its own cards (maps/capital_port.grim).
@event capital_fish_market_quiet_hour
title: The Morning Catch
when: false
pool: maps_placeholder
place: capital_fish_market
art: wave
scene: A noisy fish market on a stone quay at dawn, barrows of fish on ice, gulls wheeling, fishwives shouting prices.
text: The fish market has been open since before the sun and has no intention of being polite about it. The catch is on ice, the gulls are on the roofs and the fishwives are on everyone.
> left: Buy a hot fish pasty
  gold -tiny
  health +tiny
  say: {~Hot, peppery and wrapped in yesterday's broadsheet. You eat it on the quay with the gulls watching.|The pasty seller calls you "my love" and gives you the one with extra pastry.}
> right: Listen to the gossip
  lore +tiny
  say: {~Who's courting whom, whose boat came in light, which warehouse had the customs men in. Port Calder knows everything by breakfast.|You learn three scandals and the price of eels before you've finished walking the quay.}

@event ashby_lane_quiet_hour
title: The Crooked Lane
pool: maps_placeholder
place: ashby_lane
art: door
scene: A narrow crooked lane in an old harbour town, houses leaning together overhead, washing strung between the windows, a door with a scuffed step.
text: Ashby Lane is so narrow the houses lean on each other for company. Washing hangs across it. A woman on a step looks at your academy coat and says, "One of Corvin's?" as if Corvin collected people.
> left: Say you're a friend of his
  charm +tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: {~"Poor you," she says, and laughs, and then doesn't. "Tell him his grandad's chair's still here."|"A friend," she repeats. "That's new." She goes in before you can ask what she means.}
> right: Just walk through
  mood +tiny
  say: {~You walk the lane end to end. Two children follow you, then lose interest.|You walk on. A window above you shuts as you pass, firmly.}

@event fennick_farm_quiet_hour
title: Turnips and Tomatoes
pool: maps_placeholder
place: fennick_farm
art: leaf
scene: A small upland farm on a windy hillside, rows of turnips and staked tomatoes, a stone farmhouse with a smoking chimney.
text: The Fennick farm sits up on the windy side of the valley, all turnip rows and tomato stakes and a farmhouse built low against the weather. A goose sees you coming and makes its views known.
> left: Lend a hand in the rows
  vigor +tiny
  health -tiny
  say: {~You weed a row and get chased by the goose. A voice from the house calls that you can stay for tea.|{season == "winter": You help lift frozen turnips in the wind until your fingers stop working. Your hands smell of earth for a day.|You stake tomatoes in the wind until your arms ache. Your hands smell green for a day.}}
> right: Lean on the gate
  mood +tiny
  say: {~From the gate you can see the whole valley, the villages very small, the moor very big.|You lean on the gate and the goose leans on the other side, both of you thinking.}

@event almanac_printers_quiet_hour
title: The Almanac Press
pool: maps_placeholder
place: almanac_printers
art: paper
scene: A cramped village print shop with a hand press in the window, stacks of thin almanacs, funeral cards and notices pegged to dry on strings.
text: The printer's off the market green smells of ink and damp paper. This year's almanacs are stacked by the door, thin and cheerful: sowing days, saints' days, a good harvest forecast in very confident type.
> left: Buy an almanac
  gold -tiny
  lore +tiny
  say: {~Tides, sowing days, a remedy for warts. Every year in it is a good one.|You buy one. Flicking through on the step, you find a page number missing, as if a page had been printed and taken out.}
> right: Watch the press
  mood +tiny
  say: {~A woman with ink to the elbow works the press without looking up, and asks if you're the one from the academy.|The press thumps. Notices go up on the strings to dry: a sale of land, a lost dog, a wedding.}

# Retired (K5): the place has its own cards (maps/countryside_wide.grim).
@event countryside_ford_quiet_hour
title: The Stepping Stones
when: false
pool: maps_placeholder
place: countryside_ford
art: wave
scene: A wide shallow river ford with stepping stones, a flat-bottomed punt tied to a post, an old ferryman sitting on the bank.
text: At the ford the river runs wide and shallow over stepping stones, and an old ferryman sits by his punt for the days it doesn't. He's watching the water as if it owes him something.
> left: Cross on the stones
  vigor +tiny
  health -tiny
  say: {~You make it across with one wet boot. The ferryman nods as if he'd bet on the boot.|Halfway over a stone rocks. You don't fall, but your heart does.}
> right: Pay for the punt
  gold -tiny
  mood +tiny
  say: {~He poles you across without a word and holds out his hand for a coin. He looks at it a long time before he pockets it.|The punt is slow and dry and the ferryman hums the counting rhyme the whole way over.}

# Retired (K5): the place has its own cards (maps/countryside_wide.grim).
@event hollin_coppice_quiet_hour
title: Charcoal Smoke
when: false
pool: maps_placeholder
place: hollin_coppice
art: tree
scene: A coppiced woodland of thin straight trees and old stumps, blue charcoal smoke rising from a mound in a clearing.
text: Hollin Coppice is a wood of straight young trees growing from old stumps, cut and grown again since before the villages. Blue smoke rises from a charcoal mound in a clearing, and somebody has chalked a mark on every seventh trunk.
> left: Forage along the rides
  alchemy +tiny
  health -tiny
  say: {~Wood sorrel, a handful of mushrooms and a scratch from a bramble you'll be noticing all week.|You fill your pockets. A charcoal burner watches from his smoke and doesn't wave.}
> right: Count the chalk marks
  lore +tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: {~Every seventh tree, all the way along. When you go back to check, the first mark is on the eighth.|You count them as far as the clearing, and stop counting there.}

# Retired (K5): the place has its own cards (maps/countryside_wide.grim).
@event countryside_tarn_quiet_hour
title: The Still Water
when: false
pool: maps_placeholder
place: countryside_tarn
art: moon
scene: A small black mountain lake high on open upland, perfectly still, reflecting the sky and clouds, a student on the stony shore.
text: The tarn lies up on the upland in a cup of stone, black and so still that the clouds in it look deeper than the clouds above. Nothing lives on its shore but wind.
> left: Skim stones
  mood +small
  say: {~Seven skips. Then six. The rings go out to the far side and the tarn takes a long time to be still again.|You skim stones until your arm aches. The tarn swallows each one politely.}
> right: Sit and look into it
  lore +tiny
  mood -tiny
  say: {~You look into the water a long time. The sky down there is a little different from this one, and you can't say how.|You sit by the tarn until you're cold. It's the quietest place you've ever been.}

# Retired (K5): the place has its own cards (maps/countryside_wide.grim).
@event countryside_quarry_quiet_hour
title: The Echo
when: false
pool: maps_placeholder
place: countryside_quarry
art: rune
scene: An abandoned stone quarry with tall pale rock faces streaked with fossils, rubble below, a student calling out with cupped hands.
text: The old quarry's walls are full of fossils, shells from a sea that left before the valley had a name. The echo here is famous: call out, and the quarry answers.
> left: Call out
  mood +tiny
  say: {~You shout your name. The quarry says it back three times, the last time slightly wrong.|You call "hello". The echo answers "hello", and then, after a long wait, "again?"}
> right: Hunt for fossils
  lore +tiny
  health -tiny
  say: {~You chip out a perfect little shell and bark your knuckles doing it.|A spiral fossil the size of your palm. You carry it all the way back and give it a name.}

# Retired (K5): the place has its own cards (maps/countryside_wide.grim).
@event drovers_inn_quiet_hour
title: The Long Table
when: false
pool: maps_placeholder
place: drovers_inn
art: cup
scene: A rough low-beamed roadside inn full of drovers, tinkers and travellers at one long table, a dog asleep by the fire.
text: The Drovers' Inn has one long table, one fire and one rule, which nobody can remember. Drovers, tinkers and a man with a bear on a rope share it with whoever comes in.
> left: Sit at the long table
  charm +tiny
  gold -tiny
  say: {~You buy a round you can't afford and hear six stories, four of them true.|A tinker mends your bootlace for nothing and tells your fortune for a penny. It's mostly about weather.}
> right: Have a quiet drink by the fire
  mood +tiny
  say: {~The dog by the fire makes room for you, grudgingly. The cider is rough and warm.|You sit by the fire and let the noise go past. Somebody starts a song nobody finishes.}
